From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NickLabs Orbis <orbis@nicklabs.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:02:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: PS4 engine-activity telemetry and runtime GTT
 budget (Orbis)

Original NickLabs Orbis Graphics Engine 2.0 code for Liverpool/Gladius:

- orbis_engine_busy (sysfs, ro): busy fractions of GUI/CP/shader (SPI)/texture (TA),
  SDMA0/1, UVD and the memory controller, sampled from GRBM_STATUS / SRBM_STATUS /
  SRBM_STATUS2 (200 samples, 100 us apart). Liverpool has no powerplay, so amdgpu
  exposes no gpu_busy_percent; this replaces guesswork with first-hand register state.
- orbis_gtt_budget (sysfs, rw): the GTT domain budget enforced by amdgpu_gtt_mgr for
  system-memory-backed GPU buffers. Writable at runtime within [256 MiB,
  ttm.pages_limit]; the reader in amdgpu_gtt_mgr_new() now uses READ_ONCE. A lower value
  only affects later allocations (TTM evicts to system pages instead of failing).
  This is the runtime half of the Orbis unified-memory design: the VRAM carve-out is
  fixed by the loader, the GTT side follows the PC/GAMING/AI policy (orbis-memd).

Status: applies; not compiled or tested on hardware.
